    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2024/10/puma-deviate-nitro-elite-3-review-2024.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The larger Nitro Elite midsole feels protective and bouncy but overall slightly firm, and the very stiff plate can feel harsh over longer distances.",
        "Responsiveness: The Nitro Elite plus carbon PWRPLATE setup is very snappy with quick transitions, and the bounce becomes more aggressive as pace increases (strongest at fast efforts like 5K-10K).",
        "Stability: Although it is a neutral racer, stability is helped by near-zero torsional flex and a very stiff plate, plus a mild-to-moderately stiff heel counter and secure upper lockdown.",
        "Durability: The biggest issue is rearfoot outsole adhesion (a PUMAGRIP piece came off around 10 miles), but after re-gluing there was limited additional wear by about 25 miles and traction stayed strong on wet and dry roads."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2024/08/puma-deviate-nitro-elite-3-review-up-in.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Very high cushion-to-weight with a 40/32 mm stack (+4 mm vs v2); ride is protective and comfortable, with a slightly firmer forefoot layer feel.",
        "Responsiveness: The new aliphatic TPU Nitro Elite foam is springy with strong rebound, and the bottom-loaded carbon PWRPLATE creates a notably propulsive, snappy toe-off.",
        "Stability: Mixed overall; there is a noted slight lack of heel stability and no rigid heel counter, but PWRTAPE/upper lockdown is excellent with little to no heel movement reported.",
        "Durability: Outsole grip and wear resistance are still rated among the best, and early midsole signs are positive (no wrinkling after about 60 km), though long-term foam longevity is not yet fully proven."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/puma-deviate-nitro-elite-3-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Added foam and a 40/32 mm stack give a softer, more protective underfoot ride with better long-run comfort; heel/forefoot feel is lively rather than mushy.",
        "Responsiveness: The aliphatic TPU midsole and full-length carbon plate create strong bounce, high energy return, and a snappy, propulsive toe-off that improves at faster paces.",
        "Stability: Overall stability is a weak spot (described as slightly unstable), though upper lockdown is solid with secure heel hold, ankle-collar support, and midfoot wrap.",
        "Durability: PumaGrip is repeatedly described as very reliable/tacky for traction, and the foam is called more resilient, but explicit long-term outsole wear data is limited."
      ]
    }
